# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# User-supplied, licensed crystallographic executables must never be committed.
# SHELX, PLATON and friends are the user's own legally obtained installations. This
# repository resolves and invokes them; it never downloads, compiles, bundles or
# redistributes them.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/toolbox/*
!/toolbox/.gitkeep

# The PLATON distribution's own test data is read in place, never copied in.
/platon_instruction/TEST/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EXPERIMENTAL DATA -- NEVER COMMITTED, NEVER PUBLISHED.
#
# realdata_examples/ holds the owner's own measurements and a supervisor's unpublished
# reference structure. The complete archive, including manifests, indexes, descriptions
# and empty-directory markers, is private. Generic contracts and synthetic examples live
# outside this archive. Ignore rules do not remove files from existing Git history.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
/realdata_examples/**

# Belt and braces: raw measurement formats are refused anywhere in the tree, so a case
# dropped into the wrong folder is still not committable. Deliberately NOT listed here are
# .ins / .res / .cif -- a future hand-written synthetic fixture may legitimately
# need to be tracked; the /realdata_examples/** rule above is what protects the real ones.
*.hkl
*.hkl_od
*.cif_od
*.raw
*.img
*.rodhypix
*.esp

# Escape hatch: small, hand-authored, non-confidential fixtures may be tracked here.
!/crystalx_core/tests/fixtures/**

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local Python environments and personal configuration.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
/.env
/.env.*
/config.local.json

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build, packaging and test artefacts.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Transfer archives. These are a way of moving a tree between machines, not a release
# artefact, and must not enter version control or a distribution.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.zip
_to_delete_*

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Run workspaces. Every solve writes an immutable directory under runs/; these are the
# user's own results and belong to them, not to the repository.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
runs/
/scratch/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model weights are large and separately licensed; they are fetched, never committed.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.ckpt
*.pt
*.pth

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Machine-generated noise.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local publication controls and material excluded pending redistribution permission.
/.private_identifiers
/.private_identifiers.*
!/.private_identifiers.example
/paper_ref/
/platon_instruction/
# Owner-authorized upstream source is retained only in the private snapshot.
# Weights and source transfer archives remain excluded by the rules above.
# Any future native engine environment remains local and isolated.
/.native-engine-env/
/.local-engines/

# Upstream CrystalX code is supplied by each user and never committed here.
/crystalx_engine/
